\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 My O2 App Account Navigation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\fs21 \cf2 Scope:
\f1\b0  My O2 App\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Role:
\f1\b0  Product design, customer experience strategy\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Outcome:
\f1\b0  Halved product re-selection from 6 steps to 3 in the redesigned tariff-change and Bolt-On journeys.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 The Challenge\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 Customers faced unnecessary friction when switching between products and accounts. My role was to design a more intuitive, product-led navigation experience while working within the existing account and billing structure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 1. Built the missing system map\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I brought together billing, backend engineering, frontline retail and eCare to understand how accounts, products and billing worked, then consolidated the findings into a shared IA and billing logic map.\
The map captured different rules for finance agreements, companion devices and SIM Free Finance, rather than treating everything as one simple product hierarchy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 2. Shifted navigation from accounts to products\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I redesigned the experience around the product customers were actively managing, while keeping billing information at account level. This brought the app closer to the product-led web experience and reduced the need to switch between accounts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 3. Simplified the product view\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I replaced the carousel with a static product view and removed unnecessary hierarchy and headings, making the active product and key actions easier to find.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 4. Removed unnecessary re-selection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I challenged journeys where customers selected a product, then had to select it again. Actions such as Buy Bolt-On could retain the selected product context and take customers directly to the relevant journey.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 Outcome\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 The redesigned multi-product journey reduced re-selection from 6 steps to 3 across tariff-change and Bolt-On flows. Carrying product context through the journey removed unnecessary steps and created a simpler, more consistent experience.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0
