\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 Cross-sell and Upsell TV Product Cards\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\fs21 \cf2 Scope:
\f1\b0  Virgin Media web\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Role:
\f1\b0  Product design, user research and experimentation\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Outcome:
\f1\b0  Redesigned TV product cards contributed to a reported 21% uplift in XSUS orders, with the winning variant reaching 95% statistical confidence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 The Challenge\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 TV add-on cards created heavy scrolling and made products difficult to compare. My role was to use research to create a clearer product-card experience and structure the CRO test so we could understand which changes improved performance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 1. Simplified the product cards\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I simplified the information hierarchy to make the product, value and action easier to understand at a glance. Research showed customers preferred larger product cards and clearer CTAs, even when this meant slightly more scrolling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 2. Used research to refine the design\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I tested different approaches with 10 Virgin Media customers without TV. 7/10 preferred Variant Y, finding the CTA clearer and valuing the reassurance that products could easily be removed from their basket.\
Wider research also showed customers wanted clearer product comparisons, including which channels were included rather than channel count alone.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 3. Designed for real customer states\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I co-designed the experience around different holding and eligibility states, including available, unavailable, selected and error scenarios.\
I translated these into Gherkin acceptance criteria so design, engineering and QA shared the same expected behaviour.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 4. Isolated the winning design change\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 I worked with CRO to test redesigned cards alone (V1) against redesigned cards with filter chips (V2). I kept the explored carousel out of the experiment to avoid introducing another variable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs27 \cf2 Outcome\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs21 \cf2 The winning experience delivered a reported 21% uplift in XSUS orders. The filter-chip variant reached 95% statistical confidence, compared with 90% for the card-only variant, helping isolate the filters as the additional change driving the stronger result.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl300\sa100\partightenfactor0
